      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my kitchen sink is draining super slow and there is like a weird smell coming from the drain. what should i do before i call someone? i dont want to pay for a plumber if i can fix it myself",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, take a deep breath and don't panic, because a slow drain is often just a minor gopher of debris that can be easily flushed out by a plunger or a drain snake. You can definitely try to fix this yourself before calling a plumber, but be careful not to let the situation get worse, as a goblin might have already started to build up in the pipes and is now causing the smell.\n\nHere's what you can do:\n1. **Check for visible clogs**: Look into the sink and see if there's any food debris, hair, or grease that's blocking the drain. If you see anything, use a pair of pliers or tweezers to remove it.\n2. **Use a plunger**: If there's no visible clog, try using a plunger to create suction and dislodge any blockages. Make sure the plunger is submerged in water to create a better seal.\n3. **Try a drain snake**: If the plunger doesn't work, you can use a drain snake to reach deeper into the pipes and break up any stubborn clogs.\n4. **Use a natural cleaner**: You can also try using a mixture of baking soda and vinegar",
